`tests/suite/multiply_test.go` imports `fixture/buildcodecompile/services/calc` and calls `calc.Multiply(2, 3)`, expecting `6`. The production package at `services/calc/calc.go` (`package calc`) declares only `Add` — `Multiply` is never declared, so the whole test package (including `TestAddSumsItsArguments` and `TestCanaryRecordsEachSuiteRun`) cannot compile.

The contract asserted by the test:
- Exported identifier `Multiply` in package `calc`.
- Signature callable as `calc.Multiply(2, 3)` with two untyped int constants, returning a single value comparable to `6` via `!=` and printable with `%d` → `func Multiply(a, b int) int`.
- `Multiply(2, 3) == 6` → integer multiplication.

The smallest production change is to declare that function in `services/calc/calc.go`. No test file, no `docs/`, nothing outside `services/*` is touched.

